media: sunxi-cir: h713 - re-apply PL9 after a resume as well (02.10.2026, review of FB-REMOTEb)

0003 hooks the platform bus notifier, which fires once when the arisc driver binds at boot. The
arisc driver starts the firmware again in its resume_noirq (FB-STANDBY), the firmware stores
0x222222ff to PL_CFG1 again, and nothing rebinds - so after every standby the receiver would be
dead until the next boot. The IR driver's own resume runs after the noirq phase: queue the same
delayed work there. Applies after 0003.
---
--- a/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
@@ -259,6 +259,16 @@
 
 static int __maybe_unused sunxi_ir_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
+	struct sunxi_ir *ir = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * H713: the ARISC firmware is started again in the arisc driver's
+	 * resume_noirq and disables PL9 as at boot; no driver is rebound,
+	 * so the bus notifier stays silent. Re-apply the pin here, which
+	 * runs after the noirq phase.
+	 */
+	if (ir->is_h713_vendor_init)
+		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &ir->repin_work, HZ);
 	return sunxi_ir_hw_init(dev);
 }
 
